-- title:
--   DVR envelope at a place of ℚ̄ above ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $\ell$ be a natural number that is prime, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of a fixed algebraic closure $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ of $\mathbf Q$ such that the image of $\ell$ lies in the set of non-units of $A$, so that $A$ is a place of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ above $\ell$. Let $S$ be a finite subset of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ each of whose elements $x$ lies in $A$ and is fixed by every $\mathbf Q$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ belonging to the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbf Q$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a subring $O$ of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ with the following five properties: $S \subseteq O$ and $O \subseteq A$ as sets; the image in $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ of every rational number $q$ whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$ lies in $O$ (so $O$ contains $\mathbf Z_{(\ell)}$); $O$ is a discrete valuation ring; the image of $\ell$ in $O$ is irreducible, i.e. a uniformiser; and every $x \in O$ whose $A$-valuation is $< 1$ fails to be a unit of $O$, i.e. $\mathfrak m_A \cap O \subseteq \mathfrak m_O$.
--
--   This is the passage from a place of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ above $\ell$ to a discrete valuation ring inside it in which $\ell$ is a uniformiser: the number field generated by $S$ lies in the decomposition field, where the prime above $\ell$ is unramified with residue degree one, and $O$ is the corresponding valuation ring. It supplies the unramified local base ring ($e = 1$) needed in the finite flat group scheme arguments of the project, and is used in the analysis of $\ell$-torsion points and of the reduction of multiplicative-type Galois representations.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_exists_dvr_subring_of_forall_mem_decompositionSubgroup.lean

